        },
        {
          "doc_id": "6e73620ab6b64e90ef2c04bf0e0d6246185a2f4b1b13cab0df494496cff89b6a",
          "page": 53,
          "chunk_id": 134,
          "score": 0.015873015873015872,
          "vector_score": 0.690645114125793,
          "keyword_score": null
        },
        {
          "doc_id": "7576edb531d9848825814ee88e28b1795d3a84b435b4b797d3670eafdc4a89f1",
          "page": 45,
          "chunk_id": 62,
          "score": 0.015625,
          "vector_score": 0.6899903497149875,
          "keyword_score": null
        },
        {
          "doc_id": "6e73620ab6b64e90ef2c04bf0e0d6246185a2f4b1b13cab0df494496cff89b6a",
          "page": 52,
          "chunk_id": 133,
          "score": 0.015384615384615385,
          "vector_score": 0.6893912391248864,
          "keyword_score": null
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "answer": "Anecdotal testing of generative AI capabilities using standardized tests designed for humans (such as professional licensing exams or intelligence tests) does not guarantee system validity or reliability in those domains. This can occur because current testing approaches often focus on laboratory conditions or benchmark test datasets that may not extrapolate well to, or directly assess impacts in, real-world conditions. Furthermore, gaps between benchmarks and actual use can be exacerbated by prompt sensitivity and the broad heterogeneity of contexts of use.",
        "citations": [
          {
            "doc_id": "6e73620ab6b64e90ef2c04bf0e0d6246185a2f4b1b13cab0df494496cff89b6a",
            "page": 53,
            "quote": "For example, the anecdotal testing of GAI system capabilities through video games or standardized tests designed for humans (e.g., intelligence tests, professional licensing exams) does not guarantee GAI system validity or reliability in those domains.",
            "document_title": "NIST Generative AI Risk Management Profile",
            "source": "National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST AI 600-1, July 2024)",
            "source_url": "https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/ai/NIST.AI.600-1.pdf",
            "chunk_id": 134,
            "chunk_index": 0
          },
          {
            "doc_id": "6e73620ab6b64e90ef2c04bf0e0d6246185a2f4b1b13cab0df494496cff89b6a",
            "page": 53,
            "quote": "Current testing approaches often remain focused on laboratory conditions or restricted to benchmark test datasets and in silico techniques that may not extrapolate well to—or directly assess GAI impacts in real- world conditions.",
            "document_title": "NIST Generative AI Risk Management Profile",
            "source": "National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST AI 600-1, July 2024)",
            "source_url": "https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/ai/NIST.AI.600-1.pdf",
            "chunk_id": 134,
            "chunk_index": 0
          },
          {
            "doc_id": "6e73620ab6b64e90ef2c04bf0e0d6246185a2f4b1b13cab0df494496cff89b6a",
            "page": 53,
            "quote": "Gaps between benchmarks and real-world use of GAI systems may likely be exacerbated due to prompt sensitivity and broad heterogeneity of contexts of use.",
            "document_title": "NIST Generative AI Risk Management Profile",
            "source": "National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST AI 600-1, July 2024)",
            "source_url": "https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/ai/NIST.AI.600-1.pdf",
            "chunk_id": 134,
            "chunk_index": 0
          }
